{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And flesh in the field torn.</b> Because it is more severe than a nevelah (carcass), for it contains the venom of the predator, and it does not impart impurity, and they leave it in the field — therefore Scripture warns concerning it, unlike a nevelah. Therefore they sell it to a discerning member of the watch, and he eats it indoors, lest many stumble through it if they leave it in the field. And since it mentioned ox and sheep, which are permitted for eating, Scripture warns concerning torn flesh, lest the poor person eat it on account of his poverty." "<b>To the dog you shall cast it.</b> The lamed with patach implies 'to the dog' specifically — the matter refers to the guardian of the flock, that is, according to its plain sense. <b>אתו</b> (it) refers back to <b>בשר</b> (flesh), which is masculine."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:54.521621342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}